    <statement><p>Find the following integral.  Note that you can check your answer by
differentiation.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int\, t^{3}\mathopen{}\left(t^{4}-4\right)^{3} \,dt =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{\left(t^{4}-4\right)^{4}}{16}+C</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>w = t^{4} - 4</m>.  Then 
<m>dw = 4 t^{3}\,dt</m>, so that 
<me>\int\,t^{3} (t^{4} - 4)^{3}\,dt = 
  {1\over 4}\int\,w^{3}\,dw = {1\over 16} w^{4} + C = 
  {1\over 16} (t^{4} - 4)^{4} + C.</me>



</solution>
